    "_ow_note": "'ow' was listed here as a seventh new grapheme until 2026-08-21. It is not new at L6 - it is taught at L4 saying /oa/ (blow, snow). What arrives at L6 is the SECOND pronunciation /ow/ (cow, now, down), which is an alternative pronunciation and therefore a Shifty Sound, not a ladder grapheme. Listing it in both places put the same grapheme in the purple new-sounds band and the shifty deck at once (Lynden 2026-08-21). It stays in cumulative_graphemes from L4 onwards, so decodability is unchanged.",
